  v1:{histories:['competition','routing'],shift:'From an early stage outside the effect in some tasks toward task-dependent recurrent and thalamic influences.',meaning:'The 1985 null result and 1998 curve-tracing modulation are informative together. An early sensory representation can be modulated without becoming the sole locus of selection.'},
  v4:{histories:['competition','priority','routing','selection'],shift:'From filtering competing stimuli toward gain, population reliability and coordinated communication.',meaning:'V4 makes biased competition concrete, while FEF and pulvinar experiments constrain possible sources of bias. A fitted normalization model alone does not choose between those sources.'},
