  lip:{histories:['priority','sampling','selection'],shift:'From location-related activity toward a distributed, changing priority representation.',meaning:'Population activity, causal search deficits and rhythmic interactions constrain different aspects of LIP. Firing at one location is not an unambiguous prediction of the next attentional or saccadic choice.'},
  vpulv:{histories:['routing','competition'],shift:'From a higher-order route toward target-specific mixtures of relay, coordination and context.',meaning:'Keep the identified SC–inferior-pulvinar–MT pathway separate from V4/V1 interactions and from mouse LP→PM state signals. The grouped node is an aid to comparison, not a homogeneous nucleus.'},
  dpulv:{histories:['selection','routing'],shift:'From a broad spatial-attention impairment toward separable choice, confidence and sensory effects.',meaning:'Criterion-versus-sensitivity tests refine what inactivation establishes. Preserved discriminability in one dorsal-pulvinar task does not imply that all pulvinar territories lack perceptual functions.'},
  mdpulv:{histories:['sampling','routing'],shift:'From coordinated cortical activity toward phase-dependent interaction and brief causal interventions.',meaning:'Mediodorsal pulvinar belongs to the spatial-attention story, not the MD–PFC rule-maintenance story. Linking its theta coordination to pulvinar burst effects remains a synthesis to test.'},
  pfc:{histories:['control','monitoring','gating','priority','engagement'],shift:'From maintained goals toward population dynamics supported and reconfigured by specific circuits.',meaning:'Early frontothalamic recordings already included MD. Recent work adds causal operations and pathways; it does not discover thalamic involvement from nothing or eliminate cortical computation.'},
