  acc:{histories:['monitoring','control'],shift:'From monitoring conflict toward competing accounts of control allocation and updating after violated expectations.',meaning:'Expected value, conflict and prediction error are related explanatory ideas, not interchangeable measured signals. Projection and task specificity help distinguish their claims.'},
  sc:{histories:['orienting','routing'],shift:'From orienting and visual input toward a causal contribution to covert selection and downstream readout.',meaning:'Cortical sensory enhancement can survive SC inactivation while performance fails. The identified ascending pulvinar route reaches MT; it does not establish every SC–pulvinar arrow drawn here.'},
  bg:{histories:['orienting','gating'],shift:'From action gating toward covert selection and goal-dependent sensory filtering.',meaning:'SNr→SC inhibition, caudate attention signals and the mouse PFC–BG–TRN pathway concern different nuclei and methods. Their shared selection theme is a synthesis, not one experimentally complete loop.'},
  central:{histories:['engagement'],shift:'From broad engagement toward target-, layer- and endpoint-specific intervention studies.',meaning:'Keep state availability separate from selecting a particular stimulus. Central lateral and centromedian results, and deep-brain stimulation versus ultrasound, cannot be treated as interchangeable.'},
